{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>ישוב</b> — the word הוא serves as another servant [i.e., auxiliary], namely ישוב ירחמנו." "<b>And the sense of יכבוש</b> is inverted [from] 'our iniquities prevailed over us,' that they shall not rule over us anymore. And the mem of חטאתם — He returns to the remnant of His inheritance. And He mentioned עון and פשע and חטאת."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {1 "The phrase הפוך דברי עונות גברו מני is read hyper-literally; it may allude to a specific verse or liturgical line where iniquities 'prevail over us.' The syntax is compressed and the reference is not resolved in the text."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:20.895698662Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}